```
if (!f.bomb && this.state === 'playing') this._onMiss();
...
_onMiss() {
  this.lives = Math.max(0, this.lives - 1);
```

My edit changed the call to `_onMiss(f)` and signature, and I replaced the beginning of _onMiss. But my newString contains "this._onMiss(f);" then ... "if (fruit?.grace) return; this.lives = ..." — that's right. But wait, did oldString have `_onMiss()` followed immediately by closing brace? I wrote oldString:
